│ togi   09:48:31   tuning 9h48m   session 9h48m   31 failures · 7 crashes   last observed failure 07:34, 2h14m ago
│ ■ SOLO LIMITS  16/16 → ► PHASE 1 · cycle 1 → ○ PHASE 2 → ○ CLEAN CYCLES   1:20 left
│ HELP · 9/9 · < Journal | Main >
│ █ NAVIGATION ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
│ █
│ █ ← →        Move through the nine pages in a fixed cycle that wraps, from Main to Help and back to Main. The footer shows the page's place, such as 2/9
│ █            Cores.
│ █ ↑ ↓        Scroll a page one line. j and k do the same.
│ █ PgUp PgDn  Scroll a page by its height less one line. b, f and space do the same.
│ █ Home End   Go to the top or the end of a page. g and G do the same.
│ █ Esc, m     Go back to Main.
│ █ ?, h       Open this help. The same key on the help returns to Main.
│ █ l          Open the journal, which opens at its newest event and follows new ones. The same key on the journal returns to Main.
│ █ scroll     A page opens at its top. Only a key changes the page or its scroll, so a refresh never moves it. Main scrolls only on a screen smaller than
│ █            160x45, where it shows numbers instead of gauges.
│ █ q, Ctrl-C  Exit the dashboard; tuning itself keeps running.
│ │
│ │
│ │ THE PAGES ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
│ │
│ │ 1 Main            Which phase and how far through it, what runs now, every core's gauge and a short What happened.
│ │ 2 Cores           Each core's exact tune, now, solo, gap and failure, its role and where its failure came from.
│ │ 3 Cycle           The current phase's work list: search turns, the cycle's steps or the phase 2 round.
│ │ 4 R7 evidence     R7 request order, top requesters and which cores passed as top requester.
│ │ 5 Hunts / probes  The cause of a failure and how sure the attribution is, hunt groups, splits and probe evidence.
│ │ 6 BIOS profile    The profile to enter in BIOS, one row per CCD in slot order. A * marks an offset not yet confirmed.
│ │ 7 History         What happened, expanded, with the local date of each day.
│ │ 8 Journal         The newest 400 journal events. Scrolled back, it holds its list still and counts new events until End.
│ │ 9 Help            This page.
│ │
│ │
│ │ THE GAUGES ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
│ │
│ │ tune       The tuning profile's offset for the core: a white full-height █ bar, one cell per count, -1 at the left to -50 at the right. It is drawn from
│ │            the profile in every phase, never from what is applied. A core at 0 has an empty bar.
│ │ now        The offset observed applied to the hardware now. After a stop restores the hardware, now is 0 while tune keeps the profile. now ? means no
│ │            application was observed; it is not a zero.
│ │ red point  One full-height red █ in a lane of its own under the bar, at the depth of the recorded failure constraint. No recorded failure reads f none; a
│ │            failure at 0 reads f0 and draws no cell.
│ │ solo       The deepest offset the core confirmed alone under load. s? means none is known, and then g? too.
│ │ gap        Tune minus solo, in counts shallower than solo: tune -9 and solo -45 is gap 36. It is a number, not a verdict. A negative gap means tune is
│ │            deeper than solo.
│ │ fail       The recorded failure constraint as an offset: f-50 is -50, f none is no failure recorded.
│  ←/→  pages  9/9 Help   ↑/↓  scroll   PgUp/PgDn    Esc  Main   ?  help   q  exit dashboard
